  "notes": "USAGE:\n{断行|だんこう} implies that the action requires courage or determination, often because it is unpopular, risky, or faces resistance. It is commonly used in political and business contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {改革|かいかく}を{断行|だんこう}する (to push through reform)\n- {値上|ねあ}げを{断行|だんこう}する (to decisively implement a price increase)\n- {断行|だんこう}する{覚悟|かくご} (the resolve to take decisive action)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{実行|じっこう} (execution, carrying out) is neutral and does not imply difficulty. {決行|けっこう} means to go ahead with something despite obstacles (like bad weather), but is less focused on the boldness of the decision.",
